            <ArticleTitle>Stenting after thrombectomy with the AngioJet catheter for acute myocardial infarction.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>327-30</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The presence of massive intracoronary thrombi may contraindicate stenting. The AngioJet catheter rheolytic thrombectomy prepared the road for an easy and uneventful stenting in 2 patients with acute myocardial infarction (AMI) and thrombi. This combination provides a promising strategy for patients with AMI and angiographic evidence of massive thrombi.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
